data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11, the Cosmos DB provider **removes the sync-over-async opt-in entirely**. The synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`) and `SaveChanges()` will throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime — there is no configuration to re-enable them.

## The Fix

Convert all synchronous calls to their async counterparts:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key changes:**
- Return `Task<T>` / `Task` instead of synchronous types
- Use `ToListAsync()`, `FirstAsync()`, `CountAsync()`, `SaveChangesAsync()`
- Propagate `async/await` up through your call chain (controllers, services, etc.)

You can also remove the old `CosmosEnableSyncOverAsync` / `EnableSyncOverAsync()` configuration since it no longer has any effect.
